Sval: the Autoplay actor sends chrome only the events it knows

The actor's parent side makes a chrome event from each message of its child
side, and Sval's press of play gave the event the message's name. The name
comes from the content process and chrome trusts the event, so a content
process that was taken over could raise a chrome event of any name on the
tab's browser. The parent raises SvalMediaPressPlayed for that message and
Gecko's GloballyAutoplayBlocked for any other.

diff --git a/toolkit/actors/AutoplayParent.sys.mjs b/toolkit/actors/AutoplayParent.sys.mjs
index 6032f09bd9..563d68fbd8 100644
--- a/toolkit/actors/AutoplayParent.sys.mjs
+++ b/toolkit/actors/AutoplayParent.sys.mjs
@@ -8,7 +8,12 @@ export class AutoplayParent extends JSWindowActorParent {
     let browser = topBrowsingContext.embedderElement;
     let document = browser.ownerDocument;
     let event = document.createEvent("CustomEvent");
-    event.initCustomEvent(message.name, true, false, {
+    // The content process names the message, and chrome trusts the event.
+    let name =
+      message.name == "SvalMediaPressPlayed"
+        ? message.name
+        : "GloballyAutoplayBlocked";
+    event.initCustomEvent(name, true, false, {
       url: this.documentURI,
       userGesture: !!message.data?.userGesture,
       kind: message.data?.kind ?? "media",
